From 5704bf7937ad54d6683b5463dbc986ab37e2ae76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:41:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0044-vela-unity-vk-outside-pass: Unity's NVIDIA plugin
 (NVUnityPlugin.dll) configures its DLSS plugin events with
 renderPassPrecondition = 1 (EnsureInside;
 IUnityGraphicsVulkan::ConfigureEvent in its Vulkan device init,
 unconditional: AUDIT/r8/unity/UNITY_SIDE.md), which is why NGX Evaluate
 arrives inside a render pass. Right after a module with the base name
 NVUnityPlugin.dll is loaded (the LdrLoadDll hook and the five LoadLibrary*
 hooks, after the original load returned; also once at OptiScaler init and at
 NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_Init for a module loaded before us) its executable sections
 are scanned for C7 44 24 30 01 00 00 00 C7 44 24 34 00 00 00 00 C7 44 24 38
 09 00 00 00; exactly one hit: the 01 becomes 02 (EnsureOutside) in memory
 (VirtualProtect, restore, FlushInstructionCache), once per module handle; no
 hit, several hits, already 02: nothing changed, one line. Device job R8B with
 that byte changed in the file: scene visible (luma 67.2 vs 12.1), no
 render-pass VUIDs, upscale in the same frame. VELA_UNITY_VK_OUTSIDE=0 = off.
 Log prefix 'Vela Unity VK:'. 0043 interplay: when the change was made from a
 load hook (or the module was already 'outside'), auto mode no longer defers a
 command buffer the hooks never saw just because the game is Unity; a buffer
 the hooks saw inside a pass is still deferred; a change to an already loaded
 module does not count (it may be too late for the run). Also:
 VELA_VK_DEFER_LAYOUTS value 0 (UNDEFINED) is treated as 'no barrier' (it
 could have made a barrier with newLayout UNDEFINED). Host test
 arm64ec/tests/unity_vk_patch_test.cpp: the real plugin mapped without running
 its code: one hit, RVA 250EC, changed, protection restored, second look
 'already outside' (23 checks)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
